    "field": "Climate change impacts on coral reefs",
    "problem": "Previous global climate model projections of coral bleaching operate at a coarse spatial resolution that is inadequate to inform the local-scale conservation and management planning necessary to protect specific reefs from climate change threats.",
    "method": "This study statistically downscales global climate model projections by substituting the modeled annual cycle with a high-resolution (4-km) observed climatology to produce local-scale projections of annual severe coral bleaching timing.",
    "task": "The task is to generate statistically downscaled, high-resolution projections for the timing of annual severe coral bleaching for all global coral reefs to reveal local-scale variation and inform conservation planning under different climate scenarios.",
